      "message": "fix(post): coolant refusals name the op; no flood code, no silent dry cut\n\nFollow-ups from the coolant review (PR #147):\n\n- Every built-in post captures the section's OperationName and prefixes\n  its coolant message() with \"operation <name>:\", so a multi-op program\n  says which op asked for the code the machine lacks.\n- A Flood op on a machine whose coolant list states only other kinds\n  (Mist, Through-spindle) is refused by name, never posted as M7 or dry.\n  A shop's own name (Brine) is still its flood; an unstated list and a\n  codeless Flood entry stay silent (the unstated-limit law).\n- Coolant names compare trimmed, case-blind, spaces/underscores as\n  hyphens, so \"Through spindle\" reads; the machine editor picks from\n  machine::COOLANT_KINDS (Flood, Mist, Through-spindle, Through-tool)\n  plus a custom text name. Machine and post docs list the names.\n- Post capability flag coolantModes = true (every shipped post sets it):\n  the engine refuses, by op name, any PARAM Coolant reaching a script\n  without it, so a user post that ignores the word cannot flood an\n  Off/Mist/Through-tool op.\n- Owed tests: Fanuc Lathe per-section coolant, M88 on the shipped\n  mill-turn, the op page dropdown click path, Mist then Flood on every\n  mill post (coolant_followups.rs, coolant_tests.rs).\n\nDefault-Flood goldens unchanged (conformance green).\n\nFixes #150\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
